She dumped you. Get over it.

255
00:14:24,792 --> 00:14:27,712
But, she's the one that punched me.

256
00:14:27,795 --> 00:14:30,798
Save it. You're not the victim here
and we both know it.

257
00:14:30,882 --> 00:14:32,925
You're the one
who ignored her when she said no

258
00:14:33,009 --> 00:14:34,719
and tried to force yourself on her anyway.

259
00:14:34,802 --> 00:14:36,762
Did you think she wouldn't tell?

260
00:14:37,346 --> 00:14:38,848
Never underestimate her.

261
00:14:39,348 --> 00:14:40,850
Uh… uh…

262
00:14:45,146 --> 00:14:46,856
Sounds like class is starting.

263
00:14:47,982 --> 00:14:49,358
Oh well.

264
00:14:50,401 --> 00:14:51,652
It had been a long time

265
00:14:51,736 --> 00:14:53,696
since I cried
in front of anyone like that.

266
00:14:54,488 --> 00:14:55,865
But those tears…

267
00:14:55,948 --> 00:14:57,283
Anzu.

268
00:14:58,701 --> 00:14:59,869
Thanks so much.

269
00:15:00,870 --> 00:15:04,790
They weren't sad tears.
They were tears of pure joy.

270
00:15:04,874 --> 00:15:06,876
I had a friend who could see me.

271
00:15:08,044 --> 00:15:10,254
We're gonna be together forever, Anzu.

272
00:15:10,338 --> 00:15:11,505
Yeah, we are.

273
00:15:19,555 --> 00:15:22,058
Hey Anzu, you're the best.

274
00:15:26,437 --> 00:15:27,605
Hey, gang!

275
00:15:28,147 --> 00:15:31,067
How's your break?
Are you enjoying your summer?

276
00:15:34,153 --> 00:15:37,865
And since we're talking about summer…

277
00:15:39,283 --> 00:15:41,118
Yep! It's that time!

278
00:15:41,202 --> 00:15:42,954
Summer festival season is back!

279
00:15:43,037 --> 00:15:45,081
So what are you saying?
Do you three want to go?

280
00:15:45,164 --> 00:15:48,167
I'm gonna pass.
I can't eat any of the snacks.

281
00:15:48,250 --> 00:15:49,627
Too many people there.

282
00:15:49,710 --> 00:15:52,338
You were a little too quick
to reject the idea.

283
00:15:52,421 --> 00:15:53,923
Sounds like fun to me.

284
00:15:54,006 --> 00:15:54,840
Yes!

285
00:15:54,924 --> 00:15:57,134
You both really don't wanna go?

286
00:15:57,218 --> 00:15:58,761
-Oh yeah!
-Uh…

287
00:16:00,221 --> 00:16:02,264
He probably just wants
to take his mind off

288
00:16:02,348 --> 00:16:04,308
his team losing the big game.

289
00:16:05,059 --> 00:16:06,185
Know what? Let's go.

290
00:16:06,769 --> 00:16:08,187
You two go without me.

291
00:16:08,270 --> 00:16:09,105
-Huh?
-Huh?

292
00:16:09,188 --> 00:16:12,733
We can't go alone! What if he tries
to confess his love for me?

293
00:16:12,817 --> 00:16:14,944
No! Kazuki, you have to come!

294
00:16:15,027 --> 00:16:16,654
The more the merrier, I mean it!

295
00:16:16,737 --> 00:16:18,155
Yeah, you know she's right.

296
00:16:18,239 --> 00:16:19,407
Plus, you deserve a night off

297
00:16:19,490 --> 00:16:20,700
after working all summer.

298
00:16:20,783 --> 00:16:23,619
I won't be able to keep
my feelings secret if I'm alone with her.

299
00:16:24,912 --> 00:16:26,163
Fine, then I'll go.

300
00:16:26,247 --> 00:16:27,123
-Ah!
-Yay!

301
00:16:27,206 --> 00:16:29,000
And I'll invite Saki too.

302
00:16:29,083 --> 00:16:30,584
Great.

303
00:16:30,668 --> 00:16:32,336
And we should all wear yukatas.

304
00:16:32,420 --> 00:16:34,505
It's tradition and adds to the fun!

305
00:16:34,588 --> 00:16:37,091
I don't know how to wear those.
Can't we just dress normal?

306
00:16:37,174 --> 00:16:38,009
Oh?

307
00:16:38,592 --> 00:16:40,469
Yukata? I want to wear one.

308
00:16:40,553 --> 00:16:41,387
Really?

309
00:16:42,096 --> 00:16:43,973
I got this. Leave everything to me.

310
00:16:45,141 --> 00:16:47,393
I promise it was worth the wait!

311
00:16:47,476 --> 00:16:49,979
These are so perfect, Riri! Thank you!

312
00:16:50,062 --> 00:16:52,106
-Yay!
-You're coming with us?

313
00:16:52,189 --> 00:16:53,024
Mm-hm!

314
00:16:53,107 --> 00:16:54,942
You three look wonderful.

315
00:16:55,443 --> 00:16:57,695
How is it
Anzu looks even cuter like this?

316
00:16:57,778 --> 00:17:00,698
Hmm,
this really accentuates their hotness.

317
00:17:00,781 --> 00:17:02,700
WATER BALLOONS

318
00:17:03,451 --> 00:17:05,703
Wow, there are so many people here.

319
00:17:06,370 --> 00:17:09,040
-Hang on, do you know where Junta went?
-Huh?

320
00:17:10,041 --> 00:17:10,916
What?

321
00:17:12,043 --> 00:17:16,005
Uh. Oh, excuse me. My fault. Pardon me.

322
00:17:16,547 --> 00:17:18,549
He'll never get through
being that polite.

323
00:17:20,092 --> 00:17:22,720
-Junta!
-Oh, Anzu.

324
00:17:22,803 --> 00:17:25,973
Uh, come on.
What are you doing all the way back here?

325
00:17:28,059 --> 00:17:29,477
Oh no.

326
00:17:29,560 --> 00:17:32,480
Don't get the wrong idea here, buddy.

327
00:17:35,316 --> 00:17:36,984
Ryuya.

328
00:17:37,068 --> 00:17:39,653
Are you two on a date?

329
00:17:39,737 --> 00:17:41,739
It's gotta be a date.
You're holding hands.

330
00:17:41,822 --> 00:17:43,115
-Mm.
-Uh…

331
00:17:43,199 --> 00:17:44,825
No! I was just trying to keep Junta

332
00:17:44,909 --> 00:17:46,744
from getting lost in the crowd.
That's all.

333
00:17:47,328 --> 00:17:49,789
-Hey Anzu, these guys your friends?
-Uh…

334
00:17:49,872 --> 00:17:50,748
Oh.

335
00:17:50,831 --> 00:17:53,167
I know you. You were in our junior high.

336
00:17:53,250 --> 00:17:54,960
Whoa, it's Takamine.

337
00:17:55,044 --> 00:17:56,378
With a good-looking guy.

338
00:17:56,962 --> 00:17:59,298
See? Not a date.
We're all here together.

339
00:18:00,049 --> 00:18:01,550
-Tonta.
-Huh?

340
00:18:02,134 --> 00:18:03,552
-Huh?
-Come with me.

341
00:18:03,636 --> 00:18:05,554
-Okay.
-Who's that guy?

342
00:18:06,138 --> 00:18:08,265
Uh, who? Kazuki?

343
00:18:08,349 --> 00:18:10,684
He's just a friend from school,
that's all.

344
00:18:11,268 --> 00:18:12,728
You can't be that dense!

345
00:18:12,812 --> 00:18:13,771
What do you mean?

346
00:18:15,272 --> 00:18:16,774
I know I said I wouldn't give up,

347
00:18:17,441 --> 00:18:19,819
but low-key I'm kinda rooting
for you and her.

348
00:18:20,903 --> 00:18:23,989
So step up
and quit letting this pretty boy beat you!

349
00:18:24,073 --> 00:18:27,618
Yeah, well, Kazuki's not really
looking for a girlfriend right now.

350
00:18:27,701 --> 00:18:29,995
Or so he says.
All is fair in love and war.

351
00:18:30,079 --> 00:18:32,748
Besides, when are you gonna tell her
how you feel, anyway?

352
00:18:32,832 --> 00:18:34,750
What? Uh…

353
00:18:35,584 --> 00:18:38,921
Look, I spent three years
without seeing Anzu.

354
00:18:40,756 --> 00:18:43,384
As long as I get to hang out with her,
I'm happy.

355
00:18:44,051 --> 00:18:46,345
You know, in all those girly comics,

356
00:18:46,428 --> 00:18:49,056
the unrequited love
of a childhood friend never goes anywhere.

357
00:18:50,891 --> 00:18:52,893
-Hey, what are you two talking about?
-Mm…

358
00:18:52,977 --> 00:18:55,646
The line for the shooting game is gone.
We should get going.

359
00:18:55,729 --> 00:18:57,148
Yeah, okay.

360
00:18:57,731 --> 00:18:59,483
Bye! Let's hang again soon!

361
00:19:01,986 --> 00:19:03,904
Sorry, my dude,
but you don't stand a chance.

362
00:19:03,988 --> 00:19:06,532
Huh? Looks aren't everything.
She's not that shallow.

363
00:19:06,615 --> 00:19:09,285
Yeah, I'm not sure
he's basing it on your looks.

364
00:19:10,619 --> 00:19:13,497
Who knew it was so easy
to run into people at a festival.

365
00:19:14,123 --> 00:19:17,376
I wonder if any of the kids that you went
to junior high with are here.

366
00:19:17,877 --> 00:19:19,503
Doubt it. It's pretty far.

367
00:19:19,587 --> 00:19:22,798
That's true. They probably
wouldn't come all this way for a festival.

368
00:19:28,470 --> 00:19:30,556
I know
I should have brought my hat.

369
00:19:31,891 --> 00:19:35,519
No, I can't keep hiding behind it.
I can do this.

370
00:19:39,315 --> 00:19:41,025
Are you getting hungry yet?

371
00:19:41,108 --> 00:19:42,985
I am! Why don't we get some dinner?

372
00:19:43,068 --> 00:19:44,904
I can go for takoyaki.

373
00:19:44,987 --> 00:19:46,197
I want a loaded potato.

374
00:19:46,280 --> 00:19:48,282
Cotton candy and a candied apple!

375
00:19:48,365 --> 00:19:49,658
I want a lollipop!

376
00:19:49,742 --> 00:19:50,868
That's not dinner.

377
00:19:51,368 --> 00:19:53,454
Whatever. Let's split up
and all get our own food.

378
00:19:53,537 --> 00:19:55,372
We'll meet back up for the fireworks.

379
00:19:55,456 --> 00:19:56,957
Works for me!

380
00:20:00,044 --> 00:20:01,212
-Huh?
-Uh?

381
00:20:01,295 --> 00:20:03,172
Aren't you Kazuki's friend?

382
00:20:03,255 --> 00:20:05,466
I know, it's Makoto, isn't it?

383
00:20:05,549 --> 00:20:07,384
Yep. And you're Saki.

384
00:20:07,468 --> 00:20:08,844
Is Hosshi here with you?

385
00:20:08,928 --> 00:20:11,931
Mm. We came in a group
with Kazuki and Junta.

386
00:20:12,014 --> 00:20:14,725
Really? You're here with Hayami? So cool!

387
00:20:15,309 --> 00:20:16,810
He's even wearing a yukata.

388
00:20:16,894 --> 00:20:18,771
And I bet he looks great in it.

389
00:20:18,854 --> 00:20:20,522
Are you here with anyone?

390
00:20:20,606 --> 00:20:22,858
Not really.
I'm my sister's gofer for the night.

391
00:20:22,942 --> 00:20:25,653
I'd come hang with you guys
but it would just piss her off.

392
00:20:25,736 --> 00:20:27,655
So, tell everyone "hi" for me.

393
00:20:27,738 --> 00:20:29,323
Mm-hm, of course.

394
00:20:29,949 --> 00:20:32,952
Ah, there you are.
I thought you were in the other line.

395
00:20:34,411 --> 00:20:36,330
Oh. Hey, Saki.

396
00:20:36,914 --> 00:20:38,582
Why are you here?

397
00:20:39,166 --> 00:20:41,752
You know this chick? She's pretty cute.

398
00:20:41,835 --> 00:20:43,045
Yeah, she's my ex.

399
00:20:43,128 --> 00:20:45,297
-Not bad.
-Dude, I'm jealous.

400
00:20:45,965 --> 00:20:48,384
So, this guy here
your new boyfriend?

401
00:20:49,051 --> 00:20:50,052
No, he's a friend.

402
00:20:50,886 --> 00:20:52,513
Oh? So you're single?

403
00:20:52,596 --> 00:20:55,266
Don't bother. She's a real ice princess.

404
00:20:55,349 --> 00:20:56,392
Ooh.

405
00:20:58,269 --> 00:20:59,770
Anzu, save me.

406
00:20:59,853 --> 00:21:00,980
Uh…

407
00:21:02,147 --> 00:21:03,315
Did you hear?

408
00:21:03,399 --> 00:21:06,360
The big potato stand
has five new toppings this year.

409
00:21:06,443 --> 00:21:07,278
What?

410
00:21:07,945 --> 00:21:10,406
Hey Saki, let's go check it out!

411
00:21:15,369 --> 00:21:16,412
Huh?

412
00:21:20,833 --> 00:21:23,460
I got the feeling
you needed a way out back there,

413
00:21:23,544 --> 00:21:25,087
sorry if I overstepped.

414
00:21:25,170 --> 00:21:26,505
Mm-mm.

415
00:21:27,965 --> 00:21:29,216
Thank you.

416
00:21:29,300 --> 00:21:32,428
And I'm sorry too.
You lost your place in line for me.

417
00:21:33,012 --> 00:21:35,931
Yeah, it's no biggie.
I can always get back in line.

418
00:21:36,015 --> 00:21:36,932
Huh?

419
00:21:38,851 --> 00:21:41,770
Look! They really do have
new toppings this year.

420
00:21:42,271 --> 00:21:43,439
Wanna grab some food?

421
00:21:44,523 --> 00:21:45,649
Yeah.

422
00:21:47,901 --> 00:21:49,194
Hey!

423
00:21:49,278 --> 00:21:51,322
-You find anything good?
-Yeah.

424
00:21:51,947 --> 00:21:54,325
I guess everyone else is still in line.

425
00:21:54,408 --> 00:21:55,826
Huh?

426
00:21:57,119 --> 00:21:59,204
-You wore it.
-Huh?

427
00:21:59,288 --> 00:22:01,832
Oh, good catch!
It's the one you bought for me.

428
00:22:02,624 --> 00:22:03,834
Hmm.

429
00:22:07,129 --> 00:22:08,505
Hey, it's starting.

430
00:22:20,392 --> 00:22:23,062
We look so cute. I'm gonna post it now.

431
00:22:23,145 --> 00:22:25,356
Shouldn't you blur
the people in the background?

432
00:22:25,439 --> 00:22:27,566
You can't make anyone out. I'm sending.

433
00:22:27,649 --> 00:22:30,903
I know, let's take a picture together
and send it to Arisa.

434
00:22:30,986 --> 00:22:32,363
Uh, I don't want to be in it.

435
00:22:33,072 --> 00:22:35,366
I bet she will get a kick
out of you in a yukata!

436
00:22:35,449 --> 00:22:37,368
Huh…

437
00:22:37,993 --> 00:22:39,661
Sorry, that took forever.

438
00:22:39,745 --> 00:22:42,873
You all made it back.
Wait, when'd you get here?

439
00:22:43,499 --> 00:22:44,458
Serendipitous.

440
00:22:45,459 --> 00:22:47,461
You're slumming in here with us commoners?

441
00:22:47,544 --> 00:22:49,963
Actually, the first firework shows

442
00:22:50,047 --> 00:22:51,757
were enjoyed by nobility.

443
00:22:51,840 --> 00:22:53,842
Okay…

444
00:22:53,926 --> 00:22:56,387
Let me get a picture. Smile.

445
00:23:13,195 --> 00:23:16,031
Here we go.

446
00:23:16,115 --> 00:23:18,409
Whoa.

447
00:23:19,243 --> 00:23:20,411
-That was close.
-Uh…

448
00:23:20,494 --> 00:23:21,370
Are you okay?

449
00:23:21,995 --> 00:23:23,956
I, uh, thanks, I'm fine.

450
00:23:24,957 --> 00:23:25,874
Wait…

451
00:23:27,459 --> 00:23:29,503
-You did that on purpose!
-I know you loved it!

452
00:23:29,586 --> 00:23:32,381
-That cotton candy wasn't cheap!
-I'll buy you another one!

453
00:23:32,464 --> 00:23:34,383
How dare you make me drop it!
You owe me another one!

454
00:23:34,466 --> 00:23:36,760
-Huh?
-I bought this for you.

455
00:23:36,844 --> 00:23:38,387
What? For me?

456
00:23:39,012 --> 00:23:41,390
Thank you for always taking care
of me, Tsuchiya.

457
00:23:41,473 --> 00:23:42,891
Uh…

458
00:23:44,768 --> 00:23:45,894
Stunning.

459
00:23:47,187 --> 00:23:48,439
Y-- Yes.

460
00:23:48,981 --> 00:23:52,651
It might have been Riri's
annoying scheme that brought us together,

461
00:23:52,734 --> 00:23:56,572
but I really hope we all can come back
and do this again next year.

462
00:24:03,245 --> 00:24:04,371
I found you.

463
00:24:07,332 --> 00:24:08,834
Tsukasa, my love.

464
00:24:11,336 --> 00:24:13,046
A fanfare, please!

465
00:24:13,130 --> 00:24:15,299
And a big congratulations!

466
00:24:15,382 --> 00:24:17,426
Did you fall for my little trick?

467
00:24:17,509 --> 00:24:20,471
I bet now you don't feel like
skipping the ending, right?

468
00:24:20,554 --> 00:24:24,224
In today's world, you can watch
whatever you want at your own convenience.

469
00:24:24,308 --> 00:24:26,977
But don't you think in that process
we've also lost something?

470
00:24:27,060 --> 00:24:29,354
Don't just let things be! Come on!

471
00:24:29,438 --> 00:24:32,024
Let's go on a super-duper happy adventure!

472
00:24:32,107 --> 00:24:34,026
So I can make sure I get paid.

